# Context

## Background
.discovery/ is gitignored by design (line 31) — it holds pipeline
scratch output. This one file is the finished judge output from the
2026-09-21 GPT-6 Astra release review (Propose-Dispose pipeline):
every dismissal with its rationale (already-present, no-absolute-
score, and so on) for that announcement.

## Why This Way
Force-added with `git add -f` so the review evidence is versioned
and reviewable alongside the branch it informed. A .gitignore
negation (!.discovery/...) would not work because git does not
descend into an ignored directory.

## Gotchas
- Once tracked, gitignore no longer applies: future edits to this
  file appear as normal modifications.
- The rest of .discovery/ stays untracked.
